  "review_notes": [
    "The anchor record mixes supplied base/index data, a genuine nonzero class witness, an unlinked realization proposition/certificate and an inert label. The entire original interface and all four genuine proofs remain archived.",
    "The actual KTheoryClass.Nonzero predicate in the inspected source is inequality of a stored value to a chosen zero. Its KTheorySpace operations have no group axioms; MellKTheory and KTheoryIndex carry unlinked contract propositions. No genuine K-theory model, perfect-complex class realization, charge or critical-line theorem is constructed here.",
    "The two differently cased realization theorem names stay distinct. Their proof content projects/forwards the selected proposition. The final Euler nonzero consequence forwards the actual supplied integer nonzero witness from the base index.",
    "No complete independent type/provider for this anchor can be extracted without retaining the mixed record or adding a newly activated historical provider. Preserve the full interface rather than rewrite its fields."
  ],
